.IX Title "RRDLIST 1"
.TH RRDLIST 1 2026-08-08 1.11.0 rrdtool
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "نام (NAME)"
rrdlist \- List directories and rrd databases.
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBrrdtool\fR \fBlist\fR
[\fB\-\-daemon\fR|\fB\-d\fR\ \fIaddress\fR]
[\fB\-\-noflush\fR|\fB\-F\fR]
[\fB\-\-recursive\fR|\fB\-r\fR]
\&\fIpath\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The \fBlist\fR function provides an \*(Aqls\-like\*(Aq interface for traversing and listing
the rrd database tree.
.PP
When using the \fB\-\-daemon\fR option, the \fBlist\fR function connects to
rrdcached, the RRD caching daemon, and issues a "list" command for the given
path.
.IP \fIpath\fR 8
.IX Item "path"
The path (starting with \*(Aq/\*(Aq) with \*(Aq/\*(Aq being the rrdcached base_dir.
.IP "\fB\-\-daemon\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fIaddress\fR" 8
.IX Item "--daemon|-d address"
Address of the rrdcached daemon. If not specified, the
RRDCACHED_ADDRESS environment variable must be set (see below).  For a
list of accepted formats, see the \fB\-l\fR option in the rrdcached
manual.
.Sp
.Vb 1
\& rrdtool list \-\-daemon 127.0.0.1:42218 /cluster/nodes/node1
.Ve
.IP \fB\-\-noflush\fR|\fB\-F\fR 8
.IX Item "--noflush|-F"
When using a daemon, \f(CW\*(C`rrdtool\ list\*(C'\fR will usually flush its cache to the
disk before performing operations. This option disables cache flushing.
.IP \fB\-\-recursive\fR|\fB\-r\fR 8
.IX Item "--recursive|-r"
Make the list of rrd databases recursive.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES"
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES"
The following environment variables may be used to change the behavior of
\&\f(CW\*(C`rrdtool\ list\*(C'\fR:
.IP \fBRRDCACHED_ADDRESS\fR 4
.IX Item "RRDCACHED_ADDRESS"
If this environment variable is set it will have the same effect as specifying
the \f(CW\*(C`\-\-daemon\*(C'\fR option on the command line. If both are present, the command
line argument takes precedence.
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"
.IX Header "AUTHOR"
Sebastien Dugue <sebastien.dugue@atos.net>
